  "term": "carbamazepine",
  "definition": "Carbamazepine is a tricyclic drug related chemically to tricyclic antidepressants that has anticonvulsant and pain-relieving effects. It reduces certain nerve response activity, and it is commonly used for pain linked to trigeminal neuralgia.",
